# `CHANGELOG.md` is append-only in practice: every branch adds bullets under
# `## Unreleased`, at the same place, and `main` moves between the branch
# starting and merging. Squash merges make it worse -- the merged commit shares
# no ancestry with the branch's own, so git sees two unrelated edits to the
# same lines and stops.
#
# The resolution is always the same: keep both sides. `merge=union` is git's
# built-in driver for exactly that, so it does it rather than asking.
#
# Read the result before pushing. Union takes both sides' lines in order and
# never reports a conflict, so the merged bullets can land in either order and
# the blank line between them can be dropped. Wrong order and tight spacing are
# possible; lost content is not. Both are a two-second fix once you have looked.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
